Article 2 (Reporting of Military Service Records)
(1) Candidates for public office required to report military service records pursuant to Article 10 (1) of the Act (Reporting and Disclosure of Military Service Records of Candidates for Public Office Requiring the National Assembly's Consent to Appointment, etc.; hereinafter referred to as "candidates") shall be as follows:
1. Prime Minister;
2. Chairperson of the Board of Audit and Inspection;
3. Chief Justice of the Supreme Court and Justices of the Supreme Court;
4. President of the Constitutional Court and three Justices of the Constitutional Court elected by the National Assembly;
5. Three members of the National Election Commission elected by the National Assembly;
6. Secretary General of the National Assembly;
7. Other candidates whose appointment requires the consent of the National Assembly or who are elected by the National Assembly under any Act.
(2) A candidate under paragraph (1) shall enter the military service records prescribed in Article 3 of the Act (Persons Required to Report and Military Service Records to Be Reported) in the Report on Military Service Records of a Candidate for Public Office in attached Form 1 (hereinafter referred to as a "report") and submit the report to the Speaker of the National Assembly. In the case of a candidate requiring the consent of the National Assembly, the appointing authority shall attach the report to the motion for consent to appointment and submit it; in the case of a candidate elected by the National Assembly, the candidate shall submit it directly.
(3) The Speaker of the National Assembly shall check whether the report submitted under paragraph (2) lacks any required attached documents or contains any error in its entries, have necessary corrections or supplements made, and issue to the candidate a Receipt of Report on Military Service Records of a Candidate for Public Office in attached Form 2.
